# CrewPulse documentation system

Before implementing anything, read:

- `context/PRD.md` — scope and current phase
- `context/STACK.md` — Cloudflare DNS, Next.js, Supabase
- `context/DESIGN.md` — UI tokens
- `context/SKILLS.md` — Emil Kowalski frontend skills
- `context/ARCHITECTURE.md` — folders, layers, data flow
- `context/CLOUDFLARE.md` — DNS and hostnames
- `context/SUPABASE.md` — database platform
- `context/MARKITDOWN.md` — Microsoft MarkItDown for Excel/PDF ingest
- `context/SLOT-ADHERENCE.md` — report from `20260615 all status.xlsx`
- `context/SCHEMA.md` — tables, RLS, API contract
- `context/RULES.md` — SOLID, DRY at 4 uses, KISS, TypeScript

Rules:

- If a request is outside the current phase in `context/PRD.md`, do not implement it. Say it is out of scope.
- Docs lead. Update the relevant `context/*.md` file before adding tables, routes, or visual tokens.
- Use Obsidian wiki links `[[PRD]]` when editing files in `context/`.
- Product name is CrewPulse. Work items are work orders, not tickets.
- Do not introduce Vite/Hono as a second app, or a second database. Next.js App Router is the locked framework ([[STACK]]).
- Every implementation request uses the four-agent crew in `context/TEAM.md` (Architect asks first → Coder → Tester argues → Manager flags the CEO).
